  "description": "The OTTAVA™ Robotic Surgical System, developed by Johnson & Johnson MedTech (Auris Health, Inc.), is a soft-tissue robotic surgical platform featuring a table-integrated architecture. Four robotic arms are integrated into the operating table and stow beneath it when not in use, reducing operating room footprint. The platform features Twin Motion™ synchronized table movements, Ethicon-designed wristed instruments (including a two-in-one needle driver), an open console, and integration with J&J's Polyphonic™ digital surgery ecosystem. The U.S. FDA granted De Novo marketing authorization (DEN250068) in July 2026 for general surgery procedures.",
